{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgpvFAPe611yHGuKodZ1m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't find a bug in `LRUCache.get` (`src/lru.py:7-12`), so I haven't changed anything.\n\n`get` returns `None` for a missing key. For a present key it moves the key to the most-recent position and returns the value. All 5 tests in `tests/test_lru.py` pass, including the recency-refresh case.\n\nI did find two behaviors that could look like wrong `get` results to a user:\n\n- **Stored `None` values:** `get` returns `None` both for a missing key and for a key whose stored value is `None`, so callers can't tell the two apart. Fixing it would mean changing the API, for example adding a `default` argument or raising `KeyError`.\n- **Capacity 0 (this is in `put`, not `get`):** `put` raises `IndexError` because it calls `self.order.pop(0)` on an empty list. A caller who then reads the key back gets nothing useful.\n\nWhich inputs are users reporting? If you can share a failing example, or tell me which of the two cases above matches, I'll fix it and add a test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":568,"cache_read_input_tokens":31175,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":568},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ebf96aa-ea73-4ce6-a928-3ca0b0a4b203","uuid":"cebfe310-af0e-4e42-9a5c-d0a0fa42558b","timestamp":"2026-11-08T05:36:05.726Z","request_id":"req_011CgpvFAAziZ5J3MEXpyQdr"}
